00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.720
MILLION COLOR!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.180
TURNS!

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:27.990
<i>Before I was able to receive an order from Queen Dianna, I was summoned to meet up with Guin Rhineford.</i>

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.780
<i>Sir Guin allied himself with Gym Ghingnham in order to carry out his plans for returning to earth.</i>

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:38.530
<i>Furthermore, he intended to leave Lady Lily Borjarno stranded on the moon.</i>

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:43.580
<i>l ended up ejecting from the White Doll after having a difficult confrontation with the Turn X.</i>

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.380
<i>It reached the point where I barely made it out with my life.</i>

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:56.010
<b>Again, To the Earth.</b>

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.830
Honestly... What could those adults possibly have been thinking!?

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.110
Still, if I hadn't checked up on more of the White Doll's various functions...

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.190
...I never would've been able to escape.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.490
Gym Ghingnham and Guin Rhineford...

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:36.800
Bruno, there should be a 'boat' that Gym Ghingnham rode to get here. Wanna swipe it and use it to return to the moon?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.010
We'll be dead meat if they discover us, you know.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.390
You can reach us on the 'Incom' if you need anything.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.680
Right!

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.180
You two looking for the bathroom?

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.980
We were just going to do a ship inspection...

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.100
Since we've already finished the navigation settings.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.480
Is that so?

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.280
I guess you two do know the ship better than anyone else.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.400
That's right!

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.910
We also wanted to get a glance at the Turn X. We were never even thinking about trying to return to the moon...

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.070
Idiot!

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:08.910
I already heard the two of you talking about how you wanted to become part of Queen Dianna's Royal Guard.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.210
Get back in there, and do your jobs!

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.000
We're sorry!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.880
We've confirmed your info matches the White Palace's data.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.090
Now, for your final confirmation, what is your date of birth?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.880
December 2nd of the year 2328.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.300
Your photo identification checks out.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.800
Open up the air lock!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.180
Sheesh...

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.780
There are some important matters which I must report to Queen Dianna and her bodyguards at once!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.280
Notify the Queen!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.400
Tell her that this young man has returned!

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.990
Pass on the message that the young man is back!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.080
Oh? So you're telling me that the White Doll's cockpit detached itself and fled?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.710
Heh, this was a rather amusing discovery.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.710
That one's a SUMO cockpit.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:01.670
This shows that the humans in the Dark History were thinking along the same line as humans like us.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:06.100
Then the White Doll, no, the Turn A can still be used?

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.470
It's technical abilities should still function at the same level.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:15.690
Which means... we should be seeing a rather bright future open up to us before our very eyes, isn't that right?

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:21.690
Correct. Just think, all our technicians had to do was exchange one simple cockpit, and that allows us to control the mighty Turn A.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.070
And even the Mustache is regenerating.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:28.490
Yes. It's quite efficient. It functions just like a human body would.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.580
One with a much more cooperative personality.
- That's right.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.190
So they took the Turn A, and are now returning to the earth with the Ghingnham battle fleet, correct?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.310
They also had intended to take me back with them.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.270
This is a complete and total betrayal!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.280
They don't even bother to tell us, then ally with Ghingnham and set a course back toward Earth!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.780
I wonder what could be wrong with the normally calm and composed Sir Guin?

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.080
I too felt like Sir Guin has changed to some person that I don't even know...

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.790
Seems like all he cared about was stealing the moon's technology!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.370
If that was the case...

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.210
He could have bribed someone within Dianna Counter.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:22.500
In this case, he's focusing on the best way to suppress those below him to gain his role as ruler.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:26.800
It was for that reason that Guin also desired to begin industrialization.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.180
That in and of itself isn't necessarily wrong.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.180
However, I believe that he's now dedicated to his new goal.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.810
Aren't you angry that he left you behind!?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:40.690
I am the daughter of a politician, after all. I don't have the time to sit around and reside in anger.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.690
Right now, our most important objective is to make sure the Turn A doesn't stay in the hands of the enemy, right?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:49.570
Yes, that is correct. But how are we supposed to retrieve it?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.580
We currently don't have any ship which we can use to pursue them!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.410
We simply have to chase them and recover it.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.290
Chase them? But how?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.880
Have you let your old age cause you to forget where you currently are?

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.290
This place is my homeland!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.880
That's right, Queen Dianna.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.300
Still, isn't this a lot to ask?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.090
I don't plan to rest while there's still much to be done.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.770
I remember this road!

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.480
I used to come here with Hamet and the other people from the Canal!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.900
Really?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.610
You're acting strange, Loran.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.990
What's so strange?

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:31.990
Turn A was stolen from you, and yet you're still acting so cheerful!

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.080
Queen Dianna is here on this truck with you to help us...

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.370
You aren't like Guin, planning some sort of deception, are you?

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:43.380
Until now, Loran has only been bound by the weight of the White Doll.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.000
Now he's free of that burden.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.880
Is that the way you feel about it?

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.090
Don't you think it was a lot of pressure?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.800
No, I don't think so.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.600
Right now, Loran is the same as when we first met him.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.470
This is the real him.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.890
What's with all of you?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.770
You haven't said anything since we began to move.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.690
Have we upset you in any way?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.610
This all feels so foreboding.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.070
Foreboding?

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.570
That's right.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.580
Ghingnham has made his move too quickly.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.910
Because of that, we had to increase security around the Genganam port.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:22.370
You mean Ghingnham's remnants have closed off the port at Genganam?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.380
A television vehicle?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.300
Fran!

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.090
I would like to speak with Queen Dianna.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:34.090
Miss Fran Doll, are you currently working for this television station?

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:36.390
Yes. That's right, but...

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.470
The port has become a dangerous place.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.310
What's going on? Has another riot started?

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.770
Apparently! The people who've been supporting Queen Dianna...

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.400
...were attacked by the Ghingnham forces.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.900
Attacked?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.490
A riot?

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.490
Oh wow, so is this where we heard all those noises coming from?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.290
This destruction was caused by the Ghingnham army's mobile suits!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.790
Ghingnham's forces?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.710
What in the world is going on!?

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.380
That damned Gym...

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.800
...he didn't even spare Queen Dianna's private port.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.180
Get these civilians out of here! It's dangerous!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.890
That's... those two people from the Suicide Squadron!?

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.900
This boat's also no good...

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.270
How are we going to get back to the earth?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.780
John! Ames... Watch yourselves!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.110
Lieutenant Harry?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.790
A... are you okay?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.410
Somehow, I am.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.790
My my, what a mess!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.000
What's going to happen to the port?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.880
It was such a pretty little port...

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.590
If they want to go back to earth, why did they have to do this?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.380
<i>- To everyone who is currently at the port, please heed what I have to say!</i>

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.380
Queen Dianna!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.180
<i>Gym Ghingnham's fleet has fled for earth...</i>

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.760
Will she be coming back?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.890
<i>...and now, because of this...</i>

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:57.890
- She could be...

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.810
<i>...we were unable to prevent their terrorist like actions.</i>

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.100
<i>I, Dianna Soriel, wish to guarantee to you something.</i>

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:09.900
<i>First, I must apologize for this decision.</i>

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.280
<i>I must ask you to permit me to return to the Earth once more.</i>

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:20.780
<i>- I neither intend to abandon you, nor do I wish to sell the moon out to the Earth.</i>

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.110
- Have they arrived yet?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.280
- Lieutenant, they're still in the process of transporting that cockpit.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.780
- Can it be repaired?

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:26.370
<i>- It is my responsibility as the Queen of the Moonrace, to hold Gym Ghingnham responsible for his actions.</i>

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.410
- What's that?

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:32.210
<i>- Only after this, will the Terrans understand that we too have a right to live on earth.</i>

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.600
<i>- It is for this reason, that I must return to the war on earth one final time.</i>

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.180
I thought all of the craft had been destroyed?

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.690
So now Queen Dianna is going to defeat Gym Ghingnham...

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.190
What? Do you support Gym Ghingnham or something?

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.190
That's not what I said!

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.110
Then we'll just have to find another ship to use.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.190
That lady...

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.070
Ms. Dona, Hamet! Cent!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.580
I have no idea what Gym Ghingnham has been planning.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.210
Perhaps I'm no longer qualified to lead the Moonrace.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.710
No. The hearts of the people are behind you, Queen Dianna.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.510
If there hadn't been riots, there would be no agitation.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.800
They are all waiting to see what you, Queen Dianna, now intend to do.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.310
I await the unified future of the earth and the moon.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:31.900
Lieutenant Harry!

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.690
Her majesty is here. Submit your report.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:37.610
Yes! We've found a vessel that can take us to the Earth...

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.780
...But it will require a large amount of repair!

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.200
Understood. In that case, make it so.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.910
Have you found a ship?

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.080
Yes. The victor hasn't been decided yet!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.710
Will we be able to return to Earth?

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.710
Now we can begin our pursuit!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.210
The Royal Guard truly is amazing.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.710
It's nothing.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.510
The Royal Guard has found an extra ship? It shouldn't be flyable!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.180
The Royal Guards have also begun requesting for technicians.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.890
What's the big deal here?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.310
If we had've been ordered to blast that one, it would've happened.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.390
Then, do you think you can handle it, Kashimu?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.480
The Royal Guards' SUMOs have also gathered there, but..

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.690
We just need to keep the ship from leaving.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.980
We can take care of that.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:18.900
Just don't use the Mahiroo!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.110
Understood.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:26.200
This is what we'll use. The Zssan Team should be ready to go.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.290
It's just like I said!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:33.710
If we use these Zssan units, we'll wipe them out in a single shot! How are they, Galis?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:38.380
They've never been used in combat before, but they should be usable.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.010
We'll take these units to earth as well.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.380
We'll decide that once I give them a test run.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.010
Ghingnham Team, we'll be launching a standard formation assault, got it?

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.810
We'll try not to overdo it with the missiles.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.480
We'll be fighting underground, so just try to keep those SUMOs busy.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.200
It moves more easily than the Borjarnon...

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.620
If even their civilians use advanced units like these...

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.910
We won't be able to win this war.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.080
In that case, we should try and take a few of them back with us.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.500
Move that cargo!

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.590
Looks like Flyboy's getting angry.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:23.090
Listen to what the technician at the left hatch says, and get those installed!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:31.520
These soldiers here can't all be from the Royal Guard, can they?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.310
Most of them are civilian volunteers.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.690
They've come here for Queen Dianna's sake.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:41.320
Naturally! The House of Ghingnham betrayed us and fled for Earth!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:45.990
We'll help you fix up your ship so you can nab that bastard!

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:48.780
- Don't get in my way.
- Ahh, I'm terribly sorry!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.990
What are they doing over there?

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.000
Once you've finished that undercoating, we'll put on the detail, Donna, Cent.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.290
Eh? What sort of marking are you putting on it?

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:01.090
Queen Dianna asked us to design a suitable emblem...

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.880
We'll need to paint a larger version of this on both sides.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.720
Roger that!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.010
Be sure it can handle the proper power outlet.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.100
We've had to add an extra energy tube.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.600
Loran, bring your Core Fighter over here.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.190
We'll do some maintenance on it for you.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.980
Right! Coming right up.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.320
Hey, after that, take this to the armory for us, alright?

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.990
Oh? Okay, but where is that?

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.990
You're that SUMO's pilot yet you don't even know something so basic?

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.620
Please just tell him.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:32.620
What?

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.290
Queen Dianna!

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.790
At ease, please.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.710
Lieutenant Harry believes that this young man possesses a lot of strength.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:42.590
Otherwise he wouldn't loan a civilian his SUMO. Please treat him accordingly.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.880
Right.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.510
So he must be Loran Cehack!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.090
I have to get him to sign something!

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.510
And me, as well!

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.010
An autograph?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.310
That tickles!

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.390
Don't move, now...

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:57.890
That's great, do me too!

00:13:57.890 --> 00:13:59.600
What are you doing!?

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:02.820
Everyone else is working, but you're just goofing off?

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.990
These sisters here are the ones who manage the armory.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:09.780
Yes. Cramming all those items in a tiny place isn't easy.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.620
So THAT'S what your doing, is it?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:18.580
The girls from the earth are kinda scary...
- And rather sensitive, too!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.790
Her overall personality may be a bit weighed down by gravity...

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.800
...But she also has a gentle side.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:29.090
So THAT'S how an Armadillo is supposed to be used.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.600
Yes, this is how a WaD should be used.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:33.390
This one is called an "Armadillo".

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.810
No, it's a WaD!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.600
I think "Armadillo" sounds better!

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.020
Fine, we'll call it that.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.110
Alright, all units, prepare for departure!

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:50.110
We'll attack the area outside the harbor to lure out the SUMOs.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.910
Following that, we'll attack the ship they are trying to restore.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.000
Commander, our reports indicate Queen Dianna is leading the work being done there.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.410
However...

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:02.710
That's not possible. Her Majesty would never conduct such menial tasks.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.920
First Decoy Team, move out!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:05.920
Sir!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.310
With this combination...

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.390
...Harry and his band of idiots that couldn't accomplish jack while on earth...

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:23.690
Will be wiped out in a single blow! Let's go!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.610
Hmm? Hamet really did draw a Whale on there?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:36.910
- The shot on the other side needs to be reversed.
- No problems. We're painting this piece by hand.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.620
Loran! Loran Cehack!

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.580
Yeah? What's up?

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.290
Come on over to the deck.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.710
Okay.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.210
Pretend to be working, and hurry to me.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.510
You should be wearing your pilot suit, and be prepared to use the Core Fighter.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.100
But, won't I be discovered if I do that?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.390
I've already asked Queen Dianna and Lady Kihel to board the ship.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:01.600
I'd prefer if the people working here didn't know about this.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.100
Hey, you can't bring those in without testing them first?

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.310
But that's...

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.820
- Turn on your radio.
- Right.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.320
Is it alright to not be wearing your space suit?

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.700
Such a thing would only result in making these people panic.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.700
You're probably right.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.290
So, you were able to find Missiles of this size?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.910
I don't know if they'll be effective.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.710
Then Loran will be the one to test them?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.710
Check out Loran's Autograph.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.290
Would you like mine?

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.590
No thanks. You're fully devoted to Queen Dianna, Lieutenant.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:31.090
I'm sorry, then.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.800
The Core Fighter will be used to test some missiles.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.510
Is it the Ghingnham forces?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.390
They're using a new type of mobile suit from the Lunar Mountain Cycle.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.180
There are six in total.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.520
Six?

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.900
Ames will have the Borjarnon, And the Kapool will be John's.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.900
You're not gonna wear a pilot's suit?

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.900
Well, it's only a simple missile test run.

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.490
Clear the launch way, the Core Fighter is taking off!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.400
What?

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.700
The Core Fighter is heading out?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:57.990
Heading out where?

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.290
It's just a missile test!

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.790
Well, where's my Borjarnon currently at?

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.790
They told me some Mr. Ebans has it now.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.500
His name is Ames.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.710
That's odd... I don't see the Kapool here either.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.590
The SUMO is missing as well.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.010
That's right, they were all working a moment ago...

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.720
I'll check from the bridge.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.720
What is it?

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.190
An enemy attack?

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.520
It seems that their target is this port.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.480
Ghingnham's people seem to do nothing but fight constantly.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:34.490
It's said that if they didn't have plans to invade earth, they never would've even had a reason to set foot on it.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.490
Close the internal hatch!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.120
Opening the external hatch!

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.800
Lieutenant Harry said that one of Ghingnham's bases will be in this direction...

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.300
Loran, sweep around to guard that other hatch for us.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.800
Roger!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.800
- They're coming!
- Leave them to me!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:09.310
They're trying to lure our attention away from their actual target...

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.200
From this position, we can't really attack them, can we?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:20.990
Dummy, we only want to use this mechanical doll scout to distract the enemy's attention,

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.490
And then the soldiers will finish 'em.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:23.910
I'm not wearing a space suit...

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.500
Neither am I!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.710
I'll give you a kiss if you succeed!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:30.080
I would like that... but...

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.300
Microscopic robots?

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:40.590
They were used to bury the technology of the former space age.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.890
Would either of you like some tea?

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:48.180
They shouldn't have cut off the power to the construction site...

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.520
The data wouldn't be erased, would it?

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.900
We've created several backup copies.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.110
- Your Majesty...
- Thank you.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:59.900
We'll close in on them after all 3 units fire!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.120
Kayra, Watch my rear!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.210
You think that'll be enough?

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:18.510
Kayra!

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:29.890
That was too easy...

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.100
I get it!

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.480
There should be four left...

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.320
...there's three to each set.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.110
And the next set will be on Loran's end!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.210
Two out of the three units are just robots!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.710
Shoot for the leader!

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.590
Aim at the one a person is flying?

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.090
It's that one!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.890
The robotic ones will have a consistent pattern.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:07.100
A person is in there...

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.510
I'll do it!

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.690
Lieutenant!

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.790
Lieutenant Harry, thank you for your assistance.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.920
We've completely cleared them out...

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:38.290
...but we lost two of our own in the process.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:41.710
If we had've allowed them to enter...

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:44.300
The port would have been completely destroyed!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:48.680
Would that Spaceship have been destroyed that easily?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.100
I can't seem to locate Kayra's cockpit anywhere around here...

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.690
I wonder where it is?

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:57.400
He might've been killed, or was thrown out into space...

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.980
Don't say things like that!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.690
I'm sorry...

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:06.700
This is different from what Lost Mountain was like, but it's still pretty scary.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.620
Did you see the movie file? His SUMO was incredible!

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.290
I saw the video.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.080
But they went and battled in mechanical dolls without me!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.710
Sochie, don't be angry.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:19.000
Then was that an order from Queen Dianna?

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.710
- Yes?
- Sochie, it's all a matter of the circumstances of the moment.

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:25.720
It's not because anyone dislikes you.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.720
- Is that so...
- Of course it is!

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:34.600
- Queen Dianna... Make sure you come home soon!
- We'll pray for your success in this battle!

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:44.820
As this ship, the Whales, is on its way to earth, we'll be practicing complex maneuvers.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.280
I look forward to seeing each of you put forth your best effort!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:51.780
It is thanks to the Moonrace's cooperative spirit that we'll be able to return to earth!

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:53.490
Thank you.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:54.500
It was nothing.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.420
It was our honor to help you in the process of returning to Earth!

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:58.960
We'll do our best for you!

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:37.540
<b><i>Yama no ha tsuki wa michi</i></b>

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:37.540
<b>As the full moon, casts itself over the mountain's edge...</b>

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:44.590
<b><i>iki zuku anata no mori</i></b>

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:44.590
<b>...it spreads the breath of life spreads into the forest where you stand...</b>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.720
<b><i>Natsu kusa abite nemuru</i></b>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.720
<b>As you sleep in the summer grass...</b>

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.600
<b><i>Itooshii yokogao</i></b>

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.600
<b>...your profile is a lovely sight to behold.</b>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.690
<b><i>Kaze ni</i></b>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.690
<b>The wind...</b>

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:13.780
<b><i>LaLaLu... LaLaLu...</i></b>

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.670
<b><i>utae... hane ni</i></b>

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.670
<b>The sight of your wings, is seen...</b>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:25.170
<b><i>tsuki utsushi</i></b>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:25.170
<b>...in the moon's reflection.</b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:32.800
<b><i>Inochi kagaya kase yo</i></b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:32.800
<b>This wonderful life will shine vividly.</b>

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:46.890
<i>Ghingnham's operation ends up being even larger than the total assault that Queen Dianna had feared.</i>

00:23:46.890 --> 00:23:50.940
<i>Guin Rhineford also begins to put pressure on Keith.</i>

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:57.200
<i>Dianna and ourselves Arrive in the Whales and meet with Horace right in the middle of their forceful negotiations.</i>

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:02.540
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...<i>
Ghingnham's Invasion</i>

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:05.130
"The Wind blows in many directions."

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:08.460
<b>Ghingnham's Invasion</b>
